  "reference_python_3": "# Mountain and Valley substitution counts for the D|H fixed-point seed.\n# a(n) = number of hexagonal unit cells after n inflations.\ndef terms(N):\n    D, H = 1, 1   # n=0: one Valley dimer D and one Mountain hexagon H\n    out = []\n    for n in range(N):\n        out.append(2*D + H)      # a Valley dimer covers 2 hexagons; H covers 1\n        D, H = 2*D + H, 9*D + 5*H\n    return out\n\nprint(terms(20))\n# Equivalently: a(0)=3, a(1)=20, a(n)=7*a(n-1)-a(n-2) for n>=2.",
